    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Thiamin 100 mg IV is given to treat or prevent Wernicke encephalopathy, in intoxication (with IV fluids; many add multivitamins and magnesium) and in withdrawal."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Acamprosate, a synthetic GABA analogue, 2 g orally once a day, may decrease relapse and drinking days."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Disulfiram blocks acetaldehyde metabolism, so drinking within 12 hours causes flushing, headache and tachycardia; with high doses of alcohol, nausea and vomiting may follow. It is contraindicated in pregnancy and cardiac decompensation; 0.5 g once a day for 1-3 weeks, then 0.25 g; its use is now limited."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
